{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base","id":1465563,"title":"Technocracy Construct Design for raids or as player home base","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-27T13:58:05-07:00","id":1465563,"title":"Technocracy Construct Design for raids or as player home base","content":"What kind of process do you use to come up with a Technocracy Construct? What level of detail do you need before feeling comfortable using it in game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:18:19-07:00","id":1465898,"title":"","content":"I don't complicate myself too much. I just show my players google images of the offices and headquarters of both fictional and non-fictional organizations. Depending on the theme of the adventure I go for different examples: if it's your typical spy or crime investigating game I pick the FBI or CIA, if it's more militaristic oriented then I use military bases, and if it's full-blown fantasy or sci-fi I use Men in Black, Mass Effect, or the Control videogame. Originality is good and all, but don't bog yourself down when you have so much material to work with. You can always adapt it to meet your preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T14:11:57-07:00","id":1466050,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This approach works well for my current Construct Adventure, because the players will already have been supplied a map by a Macro-Technician mole. Likely, the small Construct will be an outpost in a realm whose denizens are hostile to Technocracy and Traditions alike. I am thinking Hollow Earth with an Etherite who didn't get the mass-defection signal, a Progenitor and It-X. Plot-wise, I'm thinking that the team was separated for a long while. </span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Another sort of open concept would be a Tourism and Diplomacy Construct. The Ascension War is a debate as much as anything. Why not showcase the best your faction has to offer and allow guests to explore that ideal place. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For a longer and more challenging infiltration adventure, I think a map is a good idea. It is funny how, back when I ran D&amp;D, I had plentiful resources for making low level dungeons, but no ability to justify why and how such dungeons came to exist. Now, I can easily explain how a Construct came to be, but have scarce resources for their design. What I am considering is to make some posts others could contribute to with the following titles: </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rooms List (simply that - security booth, lab, living quarters, hallway, etc.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Effects List (Procedures cast on the environment and architecture)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Realms List (a list of ideas for Horizon Realms</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> or other places where Constructs could be located)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Denizens List (creatures that exist in the Realm, Construct or both)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Objects List (furniture, equipment, tools, toys and weapons)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Another thing would be to search out links on labyrinth design and just post those here. All of that is if there would be enough interest. </span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T16:44:09-07:00","id":1466062,"title":"","content":"One thing that I want to point out is that if you follow the metaplot it should affect the designs of the constructs. I do, as such I have two approaches.<br /> <br /> First, my technocracy has become very &quot;down to earth&quot;, as in almost all of their bases are situated on earth, and they have been designed to rely on cutting-edge sleeper tech first to avoid magical incidents. The avatar storm put an end to the age of big and extravagant horizon bases. Nowadays, horizon bases are few and far between, with ten times the protocols and security measures that they used to have before the storm. They exist only to conduct the research and activities that absolutely can't be done on earth. So, it's either technothriller spy bases on earth or sci-fi fortresses in the horizon realms.<br /> <br /> Second, since the avatar storm has calmed down, what happened to the other horizon constructs and the people that lived there? Ah, that's where I make things really weird and surreal. My interpretation of &quot;void adaptation&quot; is that without proper protection, the horizon morphs things into their &quot;ideal&quot; or metaphysical aspects at the expense of their physical ones. So when agents travel to these constructs to conduct S&amp;R (salvage and rescue) operations, what they find is an exaggerated parody or horror version of what that construct used to stand for. Picture the oldest house in the Control videogame, the SCP headquarters (with all the cages open), or even a bootleg version of the death star.<br /> <br /> I hope these examples help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-31-2021, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T07:55:48-07:00","id":1466286,"title":"","content":"In case you're looking for a more recent example, I highly recommend the videogame <a href=\"https://bethesda.net/es/game/deathloop\" target=\"_blank\">Deathloop</a>. The whole story could be seen as a technocratic agent trapped in a broken horizon realm ruled by 7 marauders and trying to escape while being hunted by another marauder. The setting is a unique mix of styles that I didn't know was possible: Cold war brutalism, Mid century coastal village, 60's hippy festival and 70's retrofuturism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T12:33:46-07:00","id":1466316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base?p=1466286#post1466286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case you're looking for a more recent example, I highly recommend the videogame <a href=\"https://bethesda.net/game/deathloop\" target=\"_blank\">Deathloop</a>. The whole story could be seen as a technocratic agent trapped in a broken horizon realm ruled by 7 marauders and trying to escape while being hunted by another marauder. The setting is a unique mix of styles that I didn't know was possible: Cold war brutalism, Mid century coastal village, 60's hippy festival and 70's retrofuturism.</div> </div> </div> </div>You posted the Spanish link. It isn't a smart language site, it doesn't adapt to the user's language or location settings.<br /> <br /> I changed the link to the English version in this quote if someone needs, as the site didn't offered me an easy change of language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:03:26-07:00","id":1466341,"title":"","content":"I was having some monitor issues. I went on YouTube to get info on how to fix the problem. A popular video recommended deleting the driver for your graphics card and then updating Windows to get it back. Turns out, I had a legacy graphics card. I'm limited to Civ2 and Oblivion for gaming at the moment. I was just getting into Divinity: Original Sin. <br /> <br /> I watched this: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dgW2tyO05eQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dgW2tyO05eQ</a>. Some good technocratic scenery in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base?p=1466062#post1466062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I want to point out is that if you follow the metaplot it should affect the designs of the constructs. I do, as such I have two approaches.<br /> <br /> First, my technocracy has become very &quot;down to earth&quot;, as in almost all of their bases are situated on earth, and they have been designed to rely on cutting-edge sleeper tech first to avoid magical incidents. The avatar storm put an end to the age of big and extravagant horizon bases. Nowadays, horizon bases are few and far between, with ten times the protocols and security measures that they used to have before the storm. They exist only to conduct the research and activities that absolutely can't be done on earth. So, it's either technothriller spy bases on earth or sci-fi fortresses in the horizon realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>An idea I just considered is a Functional Mega-Mansion. I was watching some documentary content about the Koch Brothers, years ago. It got into the question of why there is little to no critical media attention drawn to their corporate empire and its influence over American and other governments. The answer suggested is that they regularly threw lavish parties, to which influential journalists and media moguls were always invited and often in attendance. <br /> <br /> So, I thought about a Syndicate NPC building an Earthy Construct that is a luxury home for himself with several adjacent guest houses. In terms of cutting edge mundane technology, there are all kinds of features that could be built in to facilitate coopting important sleepers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base?p=1466062#post1466062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, since the avatar storm has calmed down, what happened to the other horizon constructs and the people that lived there? Ah, that's where I make things really weird and surreal. My interpretation of &quot;void adaptation&quot; is that without proper protection, the horizon morphs things into their &quot;ideal&quot; or metaphysical aspects at the expense of their physical ones. So when agents travel to these constructs to conduct S&amp;R (salvage and rescue) operations, what they find is an exaggerated parody or horror version of what that construct used to stand for. Picture the oldest house in the Control videogame, the SCP headquarters (with all the cages open), or even a bootleg version of the death star.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of the series, &quot;The Expanse&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base?p=1466062#post1466062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope these examples help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some good ideas. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}